CM Dual-band Moxon for 10 m and 6 m, one 50 ohm feed, aluminium tubes, in free space. Design by DK7ZB:
CM https://www.qsl.net/dk7zb/Moxon/Dualband-Moxon_10+6m.htm - the dimensions below are from his table; this model is EMWS's.
CM On 10 m it is a Moxon rectangle: reflector (x = 0) and driven element (x = 1.42 m) with their tails folded towards each
CM other, 16 cm apart. On 6 m two straight tubes inside it do the work: a reflector at 0.50 m and a radiator at 1.258 m,
CM 16 cm behind the 10 m driven element and not connected to it - it is fed by that closeness ("open sleeve").
CM Tubes: 16 mm centre sections (radius 8 mm), 12 mm sides and tails, 10 mm for the 6 m elements; boom along +X, forward.
CM What nec2c makes of it, with aluminium (the LD 5 card):
CM   28.3 MHz, DK7ZB's 10 m design frequency: 55.0 + j1.5 ohms, SWR 1.10, 6.12 dBi (4.0 dBd), front to back 33 dB.
CM   50.15 MHz, his 6 m design frequency: 49.0 + j3.3 ohms, SWR 1.07, 6.56 dBi (4.4 dBd), front to back 10.7 dB.
CM   His figures are 4.0 dBd with 30 dB, and 4.38 dBd with 11 dB. Pick 6 m in the band list to sweep it.
CM   The best match lands at 28.20 MHz (under 1.5:1 from 28.00 to 28.85) and 50.12 MHz (under 1.5:1 from 49.96 to 50.28):
CM   6 m is a narrow, high-Q match by nature. Above about 50.4 MHz it is past 2:1.
CM   Efficiency 99.6 % on 10 m, 98.1 % on 6 m, where the open-sleeve coupling runs large currents in both elements.
CM DK7ZB's own SWR measurement of a built one is best at 28.5 MHz (1.04) and 50.15 MHz (1.09). The model's 6 m agrees; on 10 m
CM it sits about 1 % low. NEC-2 has no correction for stepped tube diameters, and a real one has a boom, clamps and tube
CM overlaps the model leaves out; the page says the middle tubes slide in the centre tubes for tuning, which is how to close it.
CM Every segment is at least 8.9 tube radii long, past the 8 that NEC-2's thin-wire model wants. Doubling the segments moves
CM the best match 75 kHz lower on 10 m and 50 kHz lower on 6 m and the gain by under 0.1 dB, so "Is the model converged?"
CM reads settled on 10 m and not on 6 m: there the match is so sharp that 50 kHz is 6 ohms of reactance. Treat the 6 m
CM match centre as good to about 50 kHz.
CM NEC model by ZR1JT for EMWS, from DK7ZB's published dimensions. CC0 1.0 - public domain.
